# Where the test harness writes uploads (tests/helpers/server.ts).
.test-uploads/
# BUILD_COMMIT is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# It is written by .github/workflows/deploy.yml immediately before `railway up`
# and is the only way a deployed container can know its own commit — the CLI
# uploads a tarball with no git metadata.
#
# `railway up` skips anything matching .gitignore, so listing it here (which is
# what happened, in the same commit that created it) means the workflow writes
# the file and the CLI silently refuses to upload it. /health then reports
# "unknown" forever, which is exactly the blind spot the stamp exists to close.
#
# Nothing generates it locally, so there is nothing to ignore.
